# 中频词汇 List04
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 中频词汇List04核心词汇

{{contradict}}{/ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkt/}{反驳；与...矛盾}{The new data contradicts the earlier findings.}}
{{contrary}}{/ˈkɒntrəri/}{相反的；对立的}{Contrary to expectations, the experiment succeeded.}}
{{contrast}}{/ˈkɒntrɑːst/}{对比；对照}{The report contrasts urban and rural education systems.}}
{{controversial}}{/ˌkɒntrəˈvɜːʃl/}{有争议的}{The decision to close the school proved controversial.}}
{{convene}}{/kənˈviːn/}{召集；集合}{The committee was convened to address the emergency.}}
{{conventional}}{/kənˈvenʃənl/}{传统的；常规的}{Conventional farming methods are being challenged.}}
{{converge}}{/kənˈvɜːdʒ/}{汇聚；趋同}{The two trends converge in this innovative approach.}}
{{convert}}{/kənˈvɜːt/}{转换；转变}{The old factory was converted into a community center.}}
{{cooperate}}{/kəʊˈɒpəreɪt/}{合作；配合}{The agencies cooperated to distribute relief supplies.}}
{{coordinate}}{/kəʊˈɔːdɪneɪt/}{协调；配合}{A coordinator was hired to manage the logistics.}}
{{core}}{/kɔːr/}{核心；果心}{Innovation lies at the core of the company's philosophy.}}
{{corporate}}{/ˈkɔːpərət/}{公司的；法人的}{Corporate social responsibility is increasingly important.}}
{{correlate}}{/ˈkɒrəleɪt/}{相关；关联}{Studies show that education correlates with higher income.}}
{{correspond}}{/ˌkɒrɪˈspɒnd/}{通信；对应}{The results correspond closely with our predictions.}}
{{corrupt}}{/kəˈrʌpt/}{腐败的；使腐败}{Corrupt practices undermine public trust in institutions.}}
{{craft}}{/krɑːft/}{工艺；手艺；精心制作}{The legislation was carefully crafted to address all concerns.}}
{{crucial}}{/ˈkruːʃl/}{至关重要的}{Timing is crucial when launching a new product.}}
{{cultivate}}{/ˈkʌltɪveɪt/}{培养；耕种}{The program aims to cultivate leadership skills in youth.}}
{{currency}}{/ˈkʌrənsi/}{货币；通用}{Digital currency is gaining acceptance worldwide.}}
{{curriculum}}{/kəˈrɪkjələm/}{课程；课程表}{The curriculum was redesigned to include practical skills.}}
{{debate}}{/dɪˈbeɪt/}{辩论；讨论}{The public debate over data privacy continues to intensify.}}
{{decade}}{/ˈdekeɪd/}{十年}{Over the past decade, renewable energy costs have plummeted.}}
{{dedicate}}{/ˈdedɪkeɪt/}{致力于；奉献}{She dedicated her career to fighting poverty.}}
{{defeat}}{/dɪˈfiːt/}{击败；失败}{The team suffered a narrow defeat in the final.}}
{{defend}}{/dɪˈfend/}{防御；辩护}{The lawyer defended his client with compelling arguments.}}
{{deliberate}}{/dɪˈlɪbərət/}{故意的；深思熟虑的}{The committee made a deliberate and well-informed choice.}}
{{deliver}}{/dɪˈlɪvər/}{交付；发表}{The company promises to deliver results within six months.}}
{{demand}}{/dɪˈmɑːnd/}{要求；需求}{Consumer demand for organic food continues to grow.}}
{{democracy}}{/dɪˈmɒkrəsi/}{民主；民主政治}{Democracy thrives when citizens actively participate.}}
{{demonstrate}}{/ˈdemənstreɪt/}{证明；演示}{The results demonstrate the effectiveness of the treatment.}}
